                feedID: "https://www.swiftbharat.org/#speaker-lineup-update-2026-10-26",
                url: URL(string: "https://www.swiftbharat.org/#speakers")!,
                title: "Four more speakers join Swift Bharat 2026",
                summary: "Sabesh Bharathi, Ashutosh Vashishtha, Charlie Chapman, and Kabir Oberai join the announced lineup, bringing it to 13 speakers.",
                contentText: "Meet the four latest speakers announced for Swift Bharat 2026:\n\nSabesh Bharathi — Researcher + Engineer at Conscious Engines & MLX India organizer\nAshutosh Vashishtha — Design Evangelist at Apple\nCharlie Chapman — Developer Advocate at RevenueCat, host of the Launched podcast, and creator of Dark Noise\nKabir Oberai — Founder, building an AI-native mobile development stack | Creator of xtool.sh\n\nExplore the full lineup and each speaker’s sticker on the website.\n\nSwift Bharat is not for profit. Everything from your ticket goes back into your experience. Students can email hello@swiftbharat.org for a student access code.\n\nSponsors: Platinum — RevenueCat; Gold — Conscious Engines, Logitech; Silver — Zoho, Signeasy; Community — Gratitude, Monologue by Every.",
                contentHTML: "<p>Meet the four latest speakers announced for Swift Bharat 2026:</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/speakers/sabesh-bharathi.png\" alt=\"Sabesh Bharathi\" width=\"196\" height=\"254\" /><br /><strong>Sabesh Bharathi</strong> — Researcher + Engineer at Conscious Engines &amp; MLX India organizer<br /><a href=\"https://sabesh.space\">Website</a> · <a href=\"https://x.com/sabeshbharathi\">X</a> · <a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/sabeshbharathi/\">LinkedIn</a></p>\n<p><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/speakers/ashutosh-vashishtha.png\" alt=\"Ashutosh Vashishtha\" width=\"196\" height=\"254\" /><br /><strong>Ashutosh Vashishtha</strong> — Design Evangelist at Apple<br /><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/ashutosh.ux/\">Instagram</a> · <a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/ashutosh-vashishtha-81aa74153\">LinkedIn</a></p>\n<p><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/speakers/charlie-chapman.png\" alt=\"Charlie Chapman\" width=\"196\" height=\"254\" /><br /><strong>Charlie Chapman</strong> — Developer Advocate at RevenueCat, host of the Launched podcast, and creator of Dark Noise<br /><a href=\"https://charliemchapman.com\">Website</a> · <a href=\"https://x.com/_chuckyc\">X</a> · <a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/charliemchapman/\">LinkedIn</a></p>\n<p><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/speakers/kabir-oberai.png\" alt=\"Kabir Oberai\" width=\"196\" height=\"254\" /><br /><strong>Kabir Oberai</strong> — Founder, building an AI-native mobile development stack | Creator of xtool.sh<br /><a href=\"https://ober.ai\">Website</a> · <a href=\"https://x.com/kabiroberai\">X</a> · <a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/kabiroberai\">LinkedIn</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/#speakers\">Explore the full lineup and each speaker’s sticker</a>.</p>\n<p>Swift Bharat is not for profit. Everything from your ticket goes back into your experience. If you’re a student, <a href=\"mailto:hello@swiftbharat.org?subject=Student%20access%20code%20%E2%80%94%20Swift%20Bharat%202026\">reach out for a student access code</a>.</p>\n<h2>Sponsors</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Platinum:</strong> <a href=\"https://www.revenuecat.com/\">RevenueCat</a></li><li><strong>Gold:</strong> <a href=\"https://consciousengines.com/\">Conscious Engines</a>, <a href=\"https://www.logitech.com/\">Logitech</a></li><li><strong>Silver:</strong> <a href=\"https://www.zoho.com/\">Zoho</a>, <a href=\"https://signeasy.com/\">Signeasy</a></li><li><strong>Community:</strong> <a href=\"https://www.gratefulness.me/\">Gratitude</a>, <a href=\"https://monologue.to/\">Monologue by Every</a></li></ul>",
                imageURL: nil,
                tags: ["speakers", "sponsors", "tickets", "Swift Bharat 2026"],
                dateModified: Date(timeIntervalSince1970: 1792995147.68)
            ),
            ConferencesFeedItem(
                id: UUID(uuidString: "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000514")!,
                eventID: UUID(uuidString: "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001")!,
                feedID: "https://www.swiftbharat.org/#event-guide",
                url: URL(string: "https://www.swiftbharat.org/")!,
                title: "Swift Bharat 2026 event guide",
                summary: "Event details, speaker lineup, updated two-day schedule, sponsors, and student ticket access for Swift Bharat 2026.",
                contentText: "Swift Bharat 2026 takes place on 19–20 November 2026 at Yashwantrao Chavan Centre in Mumbai. A special opening guest will start things off. Revealed live on stage. Announced speakers: Donny Wals — Indie Developer, Consultant, and Content Creator; Monika Sardjoska — Software engineer at RevenueCat & Conference organizer; Marcin Krzyzanowski — Open Source, building Notepad.exe & senior engineer GoodNotes; Hidde van der Ploeg — Better than Mustafa at everything; Natasha The Robot — Creator, Writer, Community Organizer; Nikhil Nigade — Indie iOS & macOS Developer, designing delightful apps; Kanishka Chaudhry — iOS engineer at Upstox and Apple Scholar; Josh Holtz — Odd jobs at RevenueCat, Lead maintainer of fastlane & Organizer of Deep Dish Swift; Ratnesh Jain — Indie Developer | Building CommunityTalks; Sabesh Bharathi — Researcher + Engineer at Conscious Engines & MLX India organizer; Ashutosh Vashishtha — Design Evangelist at Apple; Charlie Chapman — Developer Advocate at RevenueCat, host of the Launched podcast, and creator of Dark Noise; Kabir Oberai — Founder, building an AI-native mobile development stack | Creator of xtool.sh; Aarshad Devani — Senior AI Architect - Cobweb MENA FZ | Speaker from Logitech; Manoj Kumar — Engineering Manager at Zoho (https://x.com/manoj_ios). Manoj joins the schedule with Beyond Translation: Live Voice Cloning with Apple Technologies. The updated two-day schedule includes speaker names, talk titles, and descriptions. Day 1 opens at 9 AM, with Mustafa’s welcome at 9:50 AM. Day 2 opens at 9 AM for pre-conference mingling, with Donny’s talk at 10 AM, followed by Kabir; Nikhil + Ratnesh speak after the morning break, and Hidde opens the afternoon. Both days include a five-minute group photo before lunch. On-stage programming ends at 5:15 PM on both days. Day 1 continues with the indie app fair and networking over refreshments and snacks, and Day 2 with a final catch-up and goodbyes in our reserved outdoor space, both until 7:30 PM. Talk slots include Q&A and speaker changeover. The schedule is subject to change.\n\nEarly bird tickets are sold out. Regular tickets cost ₹5,999 and include all keynote sessions, lunch and refreshments, conference materials, and the post-conference mixer.\n\nSwift Bharat is not for profit. Everything from your ticket goes back into your experience. Students can email hello@swiftbharat.org for a student access code.\n\nSponsors: Platinum — RevenueCat; Gold — Conscious Engines, Logitech; Silver — Zoho, Signeasy; Community — Gratitude, Monologue by Every, Rork.",
                contentHTML: "<p>Swift Bharat 2026 takes place on 19–20 November 2026 at Yashwantrao Chavan Centre in Mumbai.</p>\n<h2>Opening guest</h2>\n<p><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/speakers/opening-guest.webp\" alt=\"Blurred portrait of the mystery opening guest\" width=\"196\" height=\"254\" /><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/stickers/speakers/opening-guest.webp\" alt=\"Brass inauguration lamp with a flame shaped like a swift taking flight\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" /><br /><strong>Opening guest</strong> — A special guest to start things off. Revealed live on stage.<br /><em>The first spark:</em> Every great gathering starts with a spark. A little light, a swift taking flight, and a special guest to set the day in motion.</p>\n<h2>Announced speakers</h2>\n<p><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/speakers/donny-wals.webp\" alt=\"Donny Wals\" width=\"196\" height=\"254\" /><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/stickers/speakers/donny-wals.webp\" alt=\"Dabbawala steel tiffin carrier tagged “await” with a stroopwafel on the lid\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" /><br /><strong>Donny Wals</strong> — Indie Developer, Consultant, and Content Creator<br /><a href=\"https://www.donnywals.com\">Website</a> · <a href=\"https://x.com/DonnyWals\">X</a> · <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/donnywalsdev/\">Instagram</a> · <a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/donny-wals-33660014/\">LinkedIn</a><br /><em>Dabbawala-grade await:</em> Donny wrote the book on Swift Concurrency. Mumbai’s dabbawalas deliver lakhs of lunches a day without a data race: every tiffin awaited, none lost. Stroopwafel for the flight from the Netherlands.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/speakers/monika-mateska.webp\" alt=\"Monika Sardjoska\" width=\"196\" height=\"254\" /><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/stickers/speakers/monika-mateska.webp\" alt=\"Developer in yoga tree pose on a mat, balancing an open laptop full of code on one palm\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" /><br /><strong>Monika Sardjoska</strong> — Software engineer at RevenueCat &amp; Conference organizer<br /><a href=\"https://x.com/monika_mateska\">X</a> · <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/monika.mateska/\">Instagram</a> · <a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/monika-mateska-54796b185/\">LinkedIn</a><br /><em>Tree pose, green build:</em> Monika codes and does yoga, sometimes at the same time. Balanced on one leg, laptop in one hand, build passing: peak work–life balance.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/speakers/marcin-krzyzanowski.webp\" alt=\"Marcin Krzyzanowski\" width=\"196\" height=\"254\" /><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/stickers/speakers/marcin-krzyzanowski.webp\" alt=\"Brass Indian padlock clamped onto a spiral notepad full of code\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" /><br /><strong>Marcin Krzyzanowski</strong> — Open Source, building Notepad.exe &amp; senior engineer GoodNotes<br /><a href=\"https://krzyzanowskim.com\">Website</a> · <a href=\"https://x.com/krzyzanowskim\">X</a> · <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/marcin.krzyzanowski/\">Instagram</a> · <a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/marcinkrzyzanowski/\">LinkedIn</a><br /><em>Locked and noted:</em> CryptoSwift keeps a lot of apps’ secrets safe, and now he’s building Notepad.exe. So: a trusty brass padlock on a notepad full of code.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/speakers/hidde-van-der-ploeg.webp\" alt=\"Hidde van der Ploeg\" width=\"196\" height=\"254\" /><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/stickers/speakers/hidde-van-der-ploeg.webp\" alt=\"Brushed-aluminium award cube engraved “Mustafa’s Design Award”\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" /><br /><strong>Hidde van der Ploeg</strong> — Better than Mustafa at everything<br /><a href=\"https://hidde.design\">Website</a> · <a href=\"https://x.com/hiddevdploeg\">X</a> · <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/hiddevdploeg/\">Instagram</a> · <a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/hiddevdploeg/\">LinkedIn</a><br /><em>Mustafa’s Design Award:</em> Hidde is the best at crafting delightful app experiences, and Mustafa’s favourite to win the design award (after a few others, obviously). So he gets the only cube that matters.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/speakers/natasha-the-robot.webp\" alt=\"Natasha The Robot\" width=\"196\" height=\"254\" /><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/stickers/speakers/natasha-the-robot.webp\" alt=\"Retro tin robot munching Kerala banana chips on a mangrove root\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" /><br /><strong>Natasha The Robot</strong> — Creator, Writer, Community Organizer<br /><a href=\"https://www.natashatherobot.com\">Website</a> · <a href=\"https://x.com/natashatherobot\">X</a> · <a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/natashatherobot/\">LinkedIn</a><br /><em>Powered by banana chips:</em> Natasha has spent a good stretch of time in Kerala, out by the mangroves. Every robot needs fuel, and in Kerala that’s a paper cone of crispy banana chips.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/speakers/nikhil-nigade.webp\" alt=\"Nikhil Nigade\" width=\"196\" height=\"254\" /><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/stickers/speakers/nikhil-nigade.webp\" alt=\"Rolled Mumbai newspaper with an RSS symbol in a paperboy bicycle carrier\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" /><br /><strong>Nikhil Nigade</strong> — Indie iOS &amp; macOS Developer, designing delightful apps<br /><a href=\"https://dezinezync.com\">Website</a> · <a href=\"https://x.com/dezinezync\">X</a> · <a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/nikhil-nigade-4a395b358/\">LinkedIn</a><br /><em>The original feed reader:</em> Nikhil builds Elytra, a lovingly crafted RSS reader. Mumbai’s original feed still arrives by bicycle at 6 AM, tied with string.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/speakers/kanishka-chaudhry.webp\" alt=\"Kanishka Chaudhry\" width=\"196\" height=\"254\" /><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/stickers/speakers/kanishka-chaudhry.webp\" alt=\"Kanishka in a scholar cap, holding a laptop and a diploma, as a Swift Student Challenge winner\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" /><br /><strong>Kanishka Chaudhry</strong> — iOS engineer at Upstox and Apple Scholar<br /><a href=\"https://x.com/ralasi_\">X</a> · <a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/kanishka-c/\">LinkedIn</a><br /><em>Class of Swift:</em> Kanishka is a Swift Student Challenge winner and Apple Scholar. Scholar cap on, diploma up, code on screen: ready to ship.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/speakers/josh-holtz.webp\" alt=\"Josh Holtz\" width=\"196\" height=\"254\" /><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/stickers/speakers/josh-holtz.webp\" alt=\"Auto-rickshaw marked “Fast Lane” speeding with a deep-dish pizza on its roof\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" /><br /><strong>Josh Holtz</strong> — Odd jobs at RevenueCat, Lead maintainer of fastlane &amp; Organizer of Deep Dish Swift<br /><a href=\"https://www.joshholtz.com\">Website</a> · <a href=\"https://x.com/joshdholtz\">X</a> · <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/joshdholtz/\">Instagram</a> · <a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/josh-holtz-771b582a/\">LinkedIn</a><br /><em>Deep dish, fast lane:</em> Josh maintains fastlane and runs Deep Dish Swift in Chicago. Nothing beats Mumbai traffic like an auto-rickshaw, and this one’s delivering deep dish.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/speakers/ratnesh-jain.webp\" alt=\"Ratnesh Jain\" width=\"196\" height=\"254\" /><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/stickers/speakers/ratnesh-jain.webp\" alt=\"Vintage loudspeaker horn wired to a Raspberry Pi board, with colourful speech bubbles bursting out\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" /><br /><strong>Ratnesh Jain</strong> — Indie Developer | Building CommunityTalks<br /><a href=\"https://ratnesh-jain.github.io\">Website</a> · <a href=\"https://x.com/ratneshjain1993\">X</a> · <a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/ratnesh-jain-7a2270146/\">LinkedIn</a><br /><em>Broadcasting from a Pi:</em> Ratnesh runs Swift on a Raspberry Pi (ask him at his talk) and his CommunityTalks app is powered by one. So: Mumbai’s lamp-post loudspeaker, wired straight into a Pi.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/speakers/sabesh-bharathi.png\" alt=\"Sabesh Bharathi\" width=\"196\" height=\"254\" /><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/stickers/speakers/sabesh-bharathi.webp\" alt=\"Mumbai local train with a glowing microchip engine and teal circuit traces\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" /><br /><strong>Sabesh Bharathi</strong> — Researcher + Engineer at Conscious Engines &amp; MLX India organizer<br /><a href=\"https://sabesh.space\">Website</a> · <a href=\"https://x.com/sabeshbharathi\">X</a> · <a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/sabeshbharathi/\">LinkedIn</a><br /><em>Local Intelligence:</em> Sabesh researches and builds at Conscious Engines and brings the MLX India community together. So his Mumbai local runs on a different kind of engine: a little silicon, a lot of curiosity, and room for everyone building what comes next.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/speakers/ashutosh-vashishtha.png\" alt=\"Ashutosh Vashishtha\" width=\"196\" height=\"254\" /><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/stickers/speakers/ashutosh-vashishtha.webp\" alt=\"Brass magnifying glass over a Mumbai train ticket, revealing aligned type and a rounded teal button\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" /><br /><strong>Ashutosh Vashishtha</strong> — Design Evangelist at Apple<br /><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/ashutosh.ux/\">Instagram</a> · <a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/ashutosh-vashishtha-81aa74153\">LinkedIn</a><br /><em>Mind the Details:</em> A ticket. A button. A few words in the right place. Ashutosh’s sticker celebrates the small decisions that make design feel considered, even when you’re rushing to catch the next local.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/speakers/charlie-chapman.png\" alt=\"Charlie Chapman\" width=\"196\" height=\"254\" /><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/stickers/speakers/charlie-chapman.webp\" alt=\"Podcast microphone rocket taking off beside a crescent moon with soft blue sound waves for exhaust\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" /><br /><strong>Charlie Chapman</strong> — Developer Advocate at RevenueCat, host of the Launched podcast, and creator of Dark Noise<br /><a href=\"https://charliemchapman.com\">Website</a> · <a href=\"https://x.com/_chuckyc\">X</a> · <a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/charliemchapman/\">LinkedIn</a><br /><em>Launched after dark:</em> Charlie helps developers at RevenueCat, hosts Launched, and created Dark Noise. A microphone, a launch, and a little nighttime ambience: three parts of his world, ready for liftoff.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/speakers/kabir-oberai.png\" alt=\"Kabir Oberai\" width=\"196\" height=\"254\" /><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/stickers/speakers/kabir-oberai.webp\" alt=\"Open red metal toolbox labelled xtool containing a smartphone, terminal window, and steel spanner\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" /><br /><strong>Kabir Oberai</strong> — Founder, building an AI-native mobile development stack | Creator of xtool.sh<br /><a href=\"https://ober.ai\">Website</a> · <a href=\"https://x.com/kabiroberai\">X</a> · <a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/kabiroberai\">LinkedIn</a><br /><em>The pocket workshop:</em> Kabir created xtool.sh and is building an AI-native mobile development stack. His sticker is a pocket workshop for making apps: tools within reach, ideas on the bench, and something new taking shape.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/speakers/aarshad-devani.webp\" alt=\"Aarshad Devani\" width=\"196\" height=\"254\" /><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/stickers/speakers/aarshad-devani.webp\" alt=\"Logitech-style mouse resting on a keyboard with a small AI sail\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" /><br /><strong>Aarshad Devani</strong> — Senior AI Architect - Cobweb MENA FZ | Speaker from Logitech<br /><a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/aarshaddevani\">LinkedIn</a><br /><em>Smooth sailing with AI:</em> Aarshad shows how he uses Logitech devices to move through AI workflows and get more done. A mouse, a keyboard, and a little wind in the sails.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/speakers/manoj-kumar.webp\" alt=\"Manoj Kumar\" width=\"196\" height=\"254\" /><br /><strong>Manoj Kumar</strong> — Engineering Manager at Zoho<br /><a href=\"https://x.com/manoj_ios\">X (@manoj_ios)</a></p>\n<p>Manoj’s talk: Beyond Translation: Live Voice Cloning with Apple Technologies.</p>\n<p>The updated two-day schedule includes speaker names, talk titles, and descriptions. Day 1 opens at 9 AM, with Mustafa’s welcome at 9:50 AM. Day 2 opens at 9 AM for pre-conference mingling, with Donny’s talk at 10 AM, followed by Kabir; Nikhil + Ratnesh speak after the morning break, and Hidde opens the afternoon. Both days include a five-minute group photo before lunch. On-stage programming ends at 5:15 PM on both days. Day 1 continues with the indie app fair and networking over refreshments and snacks, and Day 2 with a final catch-up and goodbyes in our reserved outdoor space, both until 7:30 PM. Talk slots include Q&amp;A and speaker changeover. The schedule is subject to change.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/#schedule\">Explore the full schedule and talk descriptions</a>.</p>\n<p>Early bird tickets are sold out. Regular tickets cost ₹5,999 and include all keynote sessions, lunch and refreshments, conference materials, and the post-conference mixer.</p>\n<p>Swift Bharat is not for profit. Everything from your ticket goes back into your experience. If you’re a student, <a href=\"mailto:hello@swiftbharat.org?subject=Student%20access%20code%20%E2%80%94%20Swift%20Bharat%202026\">reach out for a student access code</a>.</p>\n<h2>Sponsors</h2>\n<ul><li><strong>Platinum:</strong> <a href=\"https://www.revenuecat.com/\">RevenueCat</a></li><li><strong>Gold:</strong> <a href=\"https://consciousengines.com/\">Conscious Engines</a>, <a href=\"https://www.logitech.com/\">Logitech</a></li><li><strong>Silver:</strong> <a href=\"https://www.zoho.com/\">Zoho</a>, <a href=\"https://signeasy.com/\">Signeasy</a></li><li><strong>Community:</strong> <a href=\"https://www.gratefulness.me/\">Gratitude</a>, <a href=\"https://monologue.to/\">Monologue by Every</a>, <a href=\"https://rork.com/\">Rork</a></li></ul>",
                imageURL: URL(string: "https://www.swiftbharat.org/og-image.jpg")!,
                tags: ["Swift", "iOS", "Apple development", "conference", "Mumbai", "speakers", "sponsors", "tickets"],
