                title: "Day 1 schedule — 19 November 2026",
                summary: "Day 1: registration at 9 AM, welcome at 9:50 AM, speaker sessions and a surprise, then the indie app fair and networking from 5:15–7:30 PM IST.",
                contentText: "Swift Bharat 2026 Day 1 — Thursday, Nov 19, 2026\nYashwantrao Chavan Centre, Mumbai\nAll times in IST (UTC+05:30).\n\n9:00 AM–9:50 AM: Registration & Welcome (50 min)\n\n9:50 AM–10:00 AM: Mustafa — Welcome to Swift Bharat (10 min)\n\n10:00 AM–10:10 AM: Surprise Guest — Opening Talk (10 min)\n\n10:10 AM–10:50 AM: Josh — ????????????????? (40 min)\n404, not found.\n\n10:50 AM–11:30 AM: Ashutosh — Designing for iPhone Duo (40 min)\n\n11:30 AM–11:50 AM: Chai Break (20 min)\n\n11:50 AM–12:30 PM: Sabesh — Maximizing On-Device AI on Apple Silicon (40 min)\nAll of us already possess AI-powerhouses at our disposal: our Macs and iPhones. A discussion on making the most out of on-device intelligence right on Apple Platforms for AI use-cases that are private, secure and free of cost.\n\n12:30 PM–1:00 PM: Aarshad — From React Native to Native: An AI Developers’ Journey (30 min)\n\n1:00 PM–1:05 PM: Group Photo (5 min)\nEveryone together, before we head to lunch.\n\n1:05 PM–2:20 PM: Lunch (75 min)\n\n2:20 PM–3:00 PM: Natasha — The AI-Enhanced App (40 min)\nYour app doesn't need another random AI chatbot. It needs features that solve real problems your users actually care about. In this talk, we'll look beyond the obvious AI features and explore how to supercharge your apps behind the scenes.\n\n3:00 PM–3:25 PM: Kanishka — Every Render Matters: Behind the Scenes of SwiftUI (25 min)\nWhat really happens behind the scenes when a SwiftUI view updates? Explore how SwiftUI walks the view hierarchy and drives rendering, alongside practical techniques to optimise rendering and keep high-performance apps smooth under load.\n\n3:25 PM–3:50 PM: Chai Break (25 min)\n\n3:50 PM–4:30 PM: Monika — 0xdead10cc and Other Ways iOS Kills Your App (40 min)\nNot every failure shows up as a crash. Many of the worst ones are hangs, watchdog kills and terminations during suspension, and they arrive with a vague report and no clear stack trace. This talk covers real production cases: what each looked like, how we found the cause, and what fixed it.\n\n4:30 PM–5:15 PM: Surprise (45 min)\n\n5:15 PM–7:30 PM: Indie App Fair & Networking (135 min)\nShow off your app, meet fellow makers, and swap stories over refreshments and snacks.\n\nDraft schedule · Subject to change. All times in IST (UTC+05:30). Talk slots include Q&A and speaker changeover. Networking continues until 7:30 PM on both days.",
                contentHTML: "<h2>Swift Bharat 2026 Day 1 — Thursday, Nov 19, 2026</h2>\n<p>Yashwantrao Chavan Centre, Mumbai. All times in IST (UTC+05:30).</p>\n<ol>\n<li><p><strong>9:00 AM–9:50 AM: Registration &amp; Welcome</strong> (50 min)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>9:50 AM–10:00 AM: Mustafa — Welcome to Swift Bharat</strong> (10 min)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>10:00 AM–10:10 AM: Surprise Guest — Opening Talk</strong> (10 min)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>10:10 AM–10:50 AM: Josh — ?????????????????</strong> (40 min)</p><p>404, not found.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>10:50 AM–11:30 AM: Ashutosh — Designing for iPhone Duo</strong> (40 min)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>11:30 AM–11:50 AM: Chai Break</strong> (20 min)</p><p><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/stickers/chai-snacks.png\" alt=\"Chai, samosa and vada pav\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" /></p></li>\n<li><p><strong>11:50 AM–12:30 PM: Sabesh — Maximizing On-Device AI on Apple Silicon</strong> (40 min)</p><p>All of us already possess AI-powerhouses at our disposal: our Macs and iPhones. A discussion on making the most out of on-device intelligence right on Apple Platforms for AI use-cases that are private, secure and free of cost.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>12:30 PM–1:00 PM: Aarshad — From React Native to Native: An AI Developers’ Journey</strong> (30 min)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>1:00 PM–1:05 PM: Group Photo</strong> (5 min)</p><p>Everyone together, before we head to lunch.</p><p><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/stickers/group-photo.png\" alt=\"Conference friends posing for a group photo\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" /></p></li>\n<li><p><strong>1:05 PM–2:20 PM: Lunch</strong> (75 min)</p><p><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/stickers/maharashtrian-thali.png\" alt=\"Maharashtrian thali\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" /></p></li>\n<li><p><strong>2:20 PM–3:00 PM: Natasha — The AI-Enhanced App</strong> (40 min)</p><p>Your app doesn't need another random AI chatbot. It needs features that solve real problems your users actually care about. In this talk, we'll look beyond the obvious AI features and explore how to supercharge your apps behind the scenes.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>3:00 PM–3:25 PM: Kanishka — Every Render Matters: Behind the Scenes of SwiftUI</strong> (25 min)</p><p>What really happens behind the scenes when a SwiftUI view updates? Explore how SwiftUI walks the view hierarchy and drives rendering, alongside practical techniques to optimise rendering and keep high-performance apps smooth under load.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>3:25 PM–3:50 PM: Chai Break</strong> (25 min)</p><p><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/stickers/chai-snacks.png\" alt=\"Chai, samosa and vada pav\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" /></p></li>\n<li><p><strong>3:50 PM–4:30 PM: Monika — 0xdead10cc and Other Ways iOS Kills Your App</strong> (40 min)</p><p>Not every failure shows up as a crash. Many of the worst ones are hangs, watchdog kills and terminations during suspension, and they arrive with a vague report and no clear stack trace. This talk covers real production cases: what each looked like, how we found the cause, and what fixed it.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>4:30 PM–5:15 PM: Surprise</strong> (45 min)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>5:15 PM–7:30 PM: Indie App Fair &amp; Networking</strong> (135 min)</p><p>Show off your app, meet fellow makers, and swap stories over refreshments and snacks.</p><p><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/stickers/chaat-stall.png\" alt=\"Mumbai chaat stall\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" /></p></li>\n</ol>\n<p>Draft schedule · Subject to change. All times in IST (UTC+05:30). Talk slots include Q&amp;A and speaker changeover. Networking continues until 7:30 PM on both days.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/#schedule\">View the schedule on the website</a>.</p>",
                imageURL: nil,
                tags: ["schedule", "day 1", "Swift Bharat 2026"],
                dateModified: Date(timeIntervalSince1970: 1794497733.135)
            ),
            ConferencesFeedItem(
                id: UUID(uuidString: "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000516")!,
                eventID: UUID(uuidString: "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001")!,
                feedID: "https://www.swiftbharat.org/#schedule-2026-11-20",
                url: URL(string: "https://www.swiftbharat.org/#schedule")!,
                title: "Day 2 schedule — 20 November 2026",
                summary: "Day 2: pre-conference mingling at 9 AM, talks from 10 AM, Launched Live at 4 PM, and networking from 5:15–7:30 PM IST.",
                contentText: "Swift Bharat 2026 Day 2 — Friday, Nov 20, 2026\nYashwantrao Chavan Centre, Mumbai\nAll times in IST (UTC+05:30).\n\n9:00 AM–10:00 AM: Pre-Conference Mingling (60 min)\nDoors open at 9 AM. Come early, catch up with familiar faces, and meet someone new before talks begin at 10 AM.\n\n10:00 AM–10:40 AM: Donny — Outsmart Your Agents with Concurrency Skills for Humans (40 min)\nProvide your agents with some well-written skills, write smart prompts, and you can spend your days honing your Magic: The Gathering skills. Sadly, we’re not quite there yet. This talk will help you hone your Concurrency domain knowledge so you can be a more knowledgeable expert than your agent.\n\n10:40 AM–11:20 AM: Kabir — Keeping Up with the Agent-ians: Shipping Fast and with Confidence in an Agentic World (40 min)\nWhen code is commoditized, how do you stand out anymore? We’ll tackle this question through the lens of the Software Development Lifecycle in the Apple ecosystem, plus the launch of a brand new developer tool, to raise the bar on the big differentiators: pace and quality.\n\n11:20 AM–11:50 AM: Chai Break (30 min)\n\n11:50 AM–12:30 PM: Nikhil + Ratnesh — Swift on Server - Pi to Max (40 min)\nExplore how you can use Swift to write server-side code for your app’s APIs and unlock new workflows. We start small on a Pi, and scale things up to 11…\n\n12:30 PM–12:50 PM: Manoj — Beyond Translation: Live Voice Cloning with Apple Technologies (20 min)\nExplore how we’re building live translation with voice cloning using Apple technologies. Learn about our on-device approach using Apple frameworks, and MLX, the challenges we encountered, and how we’re making multilingual conversations more natural and private.\n\n12:50 PM–12:55 PM: Group Photo (5 min)\nOne more photo with the whole Swift Bharat crew.\n\n12:55 PM–2:10 PM: Lunch (75 min)\n\n2:10 PM–2:50 PM: Hidde — Shaders, Taste & Curiosity (40 min)\nWhat if great interface ideas came from the world around us, not just from apps? In this talk, I’ll show how I use Metal to turn light, glass, texture, and movement into custom experiences for Apple devices. Good examples, curiosity, and AI can help you learn shader code and try new ideas more easily. This isn’t about using shaders everywhere. It’s about building your visual taste, looking beyond familiar app designs, and creating something unusual, delightful, and uniquely yours.\n\n2:50 PM–3:30 PM: Marcin — What's Native Anyway (40 min)\n\n3:30 PM–4:00 PM: Afternoon Break (30 min)\nStretch your legs while we get ready for Launched.\n\n4:00 PM–5:00 PM: Charlie — Launched Live (60 min)\nA live recording of the Launched podcast.\n\n5:00 PM–5:15 PM: Closing Notes & Thank Yous (15 min)\n\n5:15 PM–7:30 PM: One Last Catch-Up (135 min)\nWe’ve reserved a big outdoor space for one last catch-up. Swap contacts, find someone you’ve been meaning to chat with, and say your goodbyes.\n\nDraft schedule · Subject to change. All times in IST (UTC+05:30). Talk slots include Q&A and speaker changeover. Networking continues until 7:30 PM on both days.",
                contentHTML: "<h2>Swift Bharat 2026 Day 2 — Friday, Nov 20, 2026</h2>\n<p>Yashwantrao Chavan Centre, Mumbai. All times in IST (UTC+05:30).</p>\n<ol>\n<li><p><strong>9:00 AM–10:00 AM: Pre-Conference Mingling</strong> (60 min)</p><p>Doors open at 9 AM. Come early, catch up with familiar faces, and meet someone new before talks begin at 10 AM.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>10:00 AM–10:40 AM: Donny — Outsmart Your Agents with Concurrency Skills for Humans</strong> (40 min)</p><p>Provide your agents with some well-written skills, write smart prompts, and you can spend your days honing your Magic: The Gathering skills. Sadly, we’re not quite there yet. This talk will help you hone your Concurrency domain knowledge so you can be a more knowledgeable expert than your agent.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>10:40 AM–11:20 AM: Kabir — Keeping Up with the Agent-ians: Shipping Fast and with Confidence in an Agentic World</strong> (40 min)</p><p>When code is commoditized, how do you stand out anymore? We’ll tackle this question through the lens of the Software Development Lifecycle in the Apple ecosystem, plus the launch of a brand new developer tool, to raise the bar on the big differentiators: pace and quality.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>11:20 AM–11:50 AM: Chai Break</strong> (30 min)</p><p><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/stickers/chai-snacks.png\" alt=\"Chai, samosa and vada pav\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" /></p></li>\n<li><p><strong>11:50 AM–12:30 PM: Nikhil + Ratnesh — Swift on Server - Pi to Max</strong> (40 min)</p><p>Explore how you can use Swift to write server-side code for your app’s APIs and unlock new workflows. We start small on a Pi, and scale things up to 11…</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>12:30 PM–12:50 PM: Manoj — Beyond Translation: Live Voice Cloning with Apple Technologies</strong> (20 min)</p><p>Explore how we’re building live translation with voice cloning using Apple technologies. Learn about our on-device approach using Apple frameworks, and MLX, the challenges we encountered, and how we’re making multilingual conversations more natural and private.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>12:50 PM–12:55 PM: Group Photo</strong> (5 min)</p><p>One more photo with the whole Swift Bharat crew.</p><p><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/stickers/group-photo.png\" alt=\"Conference friends posing for a group photo\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" /></p></li>\n<li><p><strong>12:55 PM–2:10 PM: Lunch</strong> (75 min)</p><p><img src=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/2026/stickers/maharashtrian-thali.png\" alt=\"Maharashtrian thali\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" /></p></li>\n<li><p><strong>2:10 PM–2:50 PM: Hidde — Shaders, Taste &amp; Curiosity</strong> (40 min)</p><p>What if great interface ideas came from the world around us, not just from apps? In this talk, I’ll show how I use Metal to turn light, glass, texture, and movement into custom experiences for Apple devices. Good examples, curiosity, and AI can help you learn shader code and try new ideas more easily. This isn’t about using shaders everywhere. It’s about building your visual taste, looking beyond familiar app designs, and creating something unusual, delightful, and uniquely yours.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>2:50 PM–3:30 PM: Marcin — What's Native Anyway</strong> (40 min)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>3:30 PM–4:00 PM: Afternoon Break</strong> (30 min)</p><p>Stretch your legs while we get ready for Launched.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>4:00 PM–5:00 PM: Charlie — Launched Live</strong> (60 min)</p><p>A live recording of the Launched podcast.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>5:00 PM–5:15 PM: Closing Notes &amp; Thank Yous</strong> (15 min)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>5:15 PM–7:30 PM: One Last Catch-Up</strong> (135 min)</p><p>We’ve reserved a big outdoor space for one last catch-up. Swap contacts, find someone you’ve been meaning to chat with, and say your goodbyes.</p></li>\n</ol>\n<p>Draft schedule · Subject to change. All times in IST (UTC+05:30). Talk slots include Q&amp;A and speaker changeover. Networking continues until 7:30 PM on both days.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.swiftbharat.org/#schedule\">View the schedule on the website</a>.</p>",
                imageURL: nil,
